<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Opensource on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/opensource/</link><description>Recent content in Opensource on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 21 Jul 2011 13:20:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/opensource/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Twitter from Ruby</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/twitter-from-ruby/</link><pubDate>Thu, 21 Jul 2011 13:20:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/twitter-from-ruby/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;Just been looking at &lt;a href="https://github.com/jnunemaker/twitter"&gt;Ruby Twitter gem by John Nunemaker&lt;/a&gt; during my lunch break.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Looking good so far, got my &lt;a href="https://dev.twitter.com/"&gt;Twitter Dev key&lt;/a&gt; setup and have made a test post from a Ruby script.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjgvmmlDSEL-um67WP3MwEAmnOrFU1QUhNK5DNhKXKIOhU8mZfVKtxPBhLOlZwkvx3BhI-gA2WmnDZk-aOmN4XgLqPu-Bx4aIlUnGqumMzsBcubXX7mIyy5ireQgOiolh6CpeVYDmZNhvs/s1600/twitter_post.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="61" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjgvmmlDSEL-um67WP3MwEAmnOrFU1QUhNK5DNhKXKIOhU8mZfVKtxPBhLOlZwkvx3BhI-gA2WmnDZk-aOmN4XgLqPu-Bx4aIlUnGqumMzsBcubXX7mIyy5ireQgOiolh6CpeVYDmZNhvs/s320/twitter_post.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;1. Tweeting from Ruby&lt;br /&gt;&#10;2......&lt;br /&gt;&#10;3. Profit!!!&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Github</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/github/</link><pubDate>Mon, 18 Jul 2011 13:59:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/github/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Finally got round to uploading some of my stuff to the &lt;a href="https://github.com/"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; site.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;If you want a laugh have a look at my code &lt;a href="http://github.com/alastairhm"&gt;alastairhm@github&lt;/a&gt; ;)&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>LinCity-NG – the open source city simulation game</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lincity-ng-open-source-city-simulation/</link><pubDate>Thu, 17 Dec 2009 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lincity-ng-open-source-city-simulation/</guid><description>&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http:/